One idea is that you are seeing the effect of trying to do I/O to a file th=
at is not a multiple of the blocksize. In theory if you have size=3D1g and =
you have 9 files then each file ends up being 1024**3/9.0 ~ 119304647.11111=
11 big (see <a href=3D"http://fio.readthedocs.io/en/latest/fio_doc.html#cmd=
option-arg-filename" target=3D"_blank">http://fio.readthedocs.io/en/latest/=
fio_doc.html#cmdoption-arg-filename</a><BR>
for where this is described). Could it be that Windows goes on to make a fi=
le that is smaller than what we were asking for?<BR>
<BR>
If this theory were right you might see a similar problem if you were only =
using 3 files.<BR>
